chx:F1 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "Background"@en ; sen0414:findingText "Chapter 17 of the 3rd edition teaches two file formats that hold text for people to read: PDF with the PyPDF package (extract text, extract images, copy pages into a new file, rotate, insert blank pages, merge a watermark or overlay, encrypt and decrypt) and Word .docx with the Python-Docx package (Document, Paragraph and Run objects, styles, run attributes, new paragraphs, headings, breaks, pictures), with the project Combine Select Pages from Many PDFs, twelve practice questions and three practice programs: PDF Paranoia, Custom Invitations and PDF Password Breaker." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01 .
chx:F2 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "Comparative analysis"@en ; sen0414:findingText "The chapter's printed PyPDF behaviours reproduce with pypdf 6.19.0 under Python 3.14.4 on a stand-in six-page PDF: append with the tuple (0, 5) gives 5 pages, with (0, 5, 2) gives 3, with the list [0, 5] gives 2 pages (page one and page six), write() returns (False, the file object), merge at position 2 works, rotating needs a multiple of 90 and raises ValueError for 45, an encrypted file reports is_encrypted True, reading its pages raises FileNotDecryptedError with the message File has not been decrypted, a wrong password gives NOT_DECRYPTED and the right one OWNER_PASSWORD, and a copy made from the decrypted reader is not encrypted and keeps all pages." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01, chx:P05, chx:P06 .
chx:F3 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "Comparative analysis"@en ; sen0414:findingText "The chapter's Python-Docx behaviours reproduce with python-docx 1.2.0 on a stand-in document: a paragraph built from three text parts has four runs, bold is None on a run that never set it and True on the one that did, add_heading(text, 0) gives the Title style and levels 1 to 9 give Heading 1 to Heading 9, a run takes the linked style Quote Char while the paragraph style Quote is refused for a run with ValueError, a page break is one w:br element of type page, add_picture with Inches(1) and Cm(4) gives a width of 914400 and a height of 1440000 units, and Document() on a PDF raises PackageNotFoundError." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01, chx:P10, chx:P14, chx:P15 .
chx:F4 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "Comparative analysis"@en ; sen0414:findingText "Project 12 as printed does not run: the loop appends to pdf_files, a name never defined, and Python 3.14.4 answers NameError: name 'pdf_files' is not defined, suggesting pdf_filenames; with that name corrected it combines A_cover.pdf, b_report.pdf and c_one.pdf into 3 pages (the pages after each first page, nothing from the one-page file), but run a second time in the same folder it reads its own combined.pdf as an input and writes 5 pages, so the program must skip its output file." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01, chx:P20 .
chx:F5 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "Comparative analysis"@en ; sen0414:findingText "Several statements of the chapter differ from the current packages: the heading levels are given as 0 to 4 and then as 1 to 9 while add_heading accepts 0 to 9 and raises ValueError outside it; the list of default style names contains List Number with a trailing space and MacroText, neither of which exists in the default template, where the names are List Number and macro; strike, double_strike, outline and rtl are listed as Run attributes but work only on run.font (assigning run.strike = True raises no error and changes nothing), while bold, italic and underline work on both; the method insert_blank_page is printed with a stray space; and the chapter says only styles of the default set or already in the document can be used, while python-docx can add a style with styles.add_style and refuses a name the file does not define with KeyError." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01, chx:P10, chx:P12, chx:P13, chx:P14, chx:P15 .
chx:F6 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "Comparative analysis"@en ; sen0414:findingText "Two optional dependencies and a default that the chapter does not mention matter in practice: page.images needs Pillow and raises ImportError otherwise, AES encryption needs the cryptography package, and encrypt() without an algorithm writes the legacy RC4 encryption (encryption dictionary version 2, revision 3) while algorithm='AES-256' writes version 5, revision 6; the pypdf documentation warns that RC4 is insecure, warns that image names can contain arbitrary characters and must be sanitised before they are used as file names, and lists AES-256-R5 as its recommendation beside the AES-256 the chapter uses." ; sen0414:cites chx:P04, chx:P06, chx:P08, chx:P09 .
chx:F7 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "Comparative analysis"@en ; sen0414:findingText "Text extraction is weaker than the chapter's tone suggests and the gap is documented: the pages' texts are run together with no separator when they are added one after another as the chapter does, pypdf says post-processing is outside its scope and offers recipes whose dehyphenation leaves a space in follow ing when the row ends in a space and a hyphen, the pdfminer.six fallback returns form-feed-separated pages (for the stand-in PDF 'Page one text', two newlines, a form feed, 'Page two text'), and a PDF that holds only images yields little text without OCR." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01, chx:P02, chx:P03, chx:P16 .
chx:F8 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "Contemporary developments"@en ; sen0414:findingText "The packages have moved on since the chapter's examples: PdfWriter.append takes the pages to copy as a keyword pages (its second positional parameter is now called outline_item, and a tuple given there is still read as a page range), PdfWriter can start from a reader with clone_from, merge_transformed_page can scale or move a stamp, python-docx has add_page_break, add_table and styles.add_style, a character can be told from a paragraph style by the style's type, and the package named docx on the Python Package Index is a different, older project (0.2.4) from python-docx (1.2.0), as the chapter warns." ; sen0414:cites chx:P05, chx:P07, chx:P10, chx:P13, chx:P17 .
chx:F9 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "Conclusion"@en ; sen0414:findingText "For an advanced course, chapter 17 is best taught as a limit on what can be automated: a PDF is a page description made for display and a .docx is a zip of XML parts, so a program can copy, reorder, rotate, stamp, encrypt, read the paragraphs and runs of and append to such files, but cannot reliably recover reading order, paragraphs or tables from a PDF and cannot edit a Word document in the middle without care; the chapter's printed outputs hold, and optional dependencies, the defaults of encryption, the rerun trap of Project 12, file-name hygiene, style handling and human review of every extraction are what the chapter leaves for the course to add." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01, chx:P02, chx:P05, chx:P06, chx:P11, chx:P12, chx:P18, chx:P25 .
chx:Scorecard a sen0414:QualityScorecard ; rdfs:label "Quality scorecard"@en ; sen0414:topicCoverage "55 primary-source concepts inventoried from the textbook ontology." ; sen0414:citationStrength "25 sources, all opened and verified at 2026-10-01T12:00:00; 20 cited by findings." ; sen0414:methodologyCompliance "RDODI procedure v1.6.0 Stage 1." ; sen0414:reproducibility "Every source is a stable public URL; every claim names its sources." .
